text:
Coleslaw and baked beans are both excellent choices—coleslaw can be mixed a day ahead and stored cold, while beans stay flavorful after hours on the grill. Add a chilled pasta salad made with rotini and cherry tomatoes; it travels well and feeds the crowd without reheating. Corn on the cob grills quickly and tastes great fresh off the coals.  

Crows handle leftovers differently than people. In the wild, American crows cache food like walnuts and meat scraps, then return days later to retrieve them once the flavor mellows. Use cafeteria-style containers to label and chill sides the night before, then simply transfer them to a serving platter when you’re ready to serve.  

For a refreshing twist, try a cucumber-tomato salad dressed with lemon vinaigrette;
